On Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:16:36 -0700, Pat Maddox wrote:
> Add doc/guides/patch-workflow.org with concise documentation for how to
> use the system. Base the interface off the code that has been committed,
> not the descriptions or notes.

Posted as "[PATCH] doc: Add a guide to the patch workflow" [1].

I took the interface from trunk and from the Justfile on mail, and
checked each command against the script that implements it rather
than against the zib.  The guide has these sections:

- model: the two bookmarks, the two workspaces, upstream and
  submissions
- setup: the notmuch package and the settings it depends on, the jail
  bootstrap, and Emacs delivery
- tags: what sent, inbox and replied mean, and how a message leaves
  the inbox
- sending: maildir-deliver.sh, format-patch.sh and just commit-mail
- one section each for contributor, moderator and maintainer, with
  just fetch/summary/advance/push for the moderator and just am for
  the maintainer

Two places where the code and the notes disagree:

- The zib says just index runs notmuch new in the mail workspace.  No
  such recipe exists, so the guide says notmuch new.
- doc/mail-workflow.md describes an older setup.  The patch notes
  list what in it is stale.  I did not touch it in this patch.

Work that is only on the list is left out, such as archiving, the
committed tag and just process-email.

> This is documentation intended for a
> skilled operator, based on the reality of the current implementation.

It is written for an operator who knows jj and notmuch.  It gives
commands and states the constraints, without walkthroughs.

I committed the patch post with just commit-mail, so it is titled
"msg:", as you asked in "Use msg: prefix for messages posted to the
list" [2].  I will answer that thread itself on its own pass.

